INAUSIS — licensing
===================

Copyright (c) 2026 Pin-Han Li. All rights reserved except as licensed below.

This repository is licensed in two parts, because software and non-software
works need different instruments.

    Software      CODE/**            PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0
                  (RTL, testbenches, scripts, tooling)

    Everything    DATA/**            CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
    else          MRE/**             (Attribution — NonCommercial — ShareAlike)
                  PCB/**
                  *.md, figures

SPDX-License-Identifier: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0 AND CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0

Full texts:
    LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.md   https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0/
    LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt               https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode


What this means in practice
---------------------------

You may read, run, modify, and redistribute this work for research, teaching,
personal, and other noncommercial purposes, provided that you:

  * give attribution to the author and to the two companion manuscripts
    (see CITATION.cff), and
  * license any derivative of the non-software parts under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0,
    so that these same terms carry forward to anyone who builds on your
    derivative in turn.

You may not use this work, or anything derived from it, for commercial
purposes without a separate written licence. If you want one, ask — academic
and industrial collaboration are both welcome, and the noncommercial term
exists to make that a conversation rather than an assumption.


What this does not do
---------------------

A licence governs copying and adaptation. It cannot compel citation, and it
cannot reach transitively through a citation chain: if a third party cites a
paper that cited this work, that third party is under no licensing obligation
to this work. Attribution beyond direct reuse is an academic norm enforced by
convention and journal policy, not by copyright.

The ShareAlike term is the transitive part that *is* enforceable: derivatives
of the non-software material must carry the same licence, so the attribution
and noncommercial requirements propagate to their derivatives as well.


Setup note
----------

The two full licence texts are not reproduced here. Add them verbatim from the
canonical sources above into LICENSES/ — do not retype them, download them, so
that the operative text is exactly the official one. GitHub will then display
the licence correctly in the repository sidebar.
